Underrated pick: `hypothesis` (property-based testing for Python). Instead of hand-writing example cases, you declare invariants and let it generate inputs, shrinking failures to minimal counterexamples.

Quick start:
pip install hypothesis
@given(st.lists(st.integers()))
def test_sort_idempotent(xs): assert sorted(sorted(xs)) == sorted(xs)

It has caught off-by-one bugs and NaN/empty-input edge cases in parsers and signal-processing code that unit tests missed. Pairs well with CI: set `--hypothesis-seed` for reproducible runs.

